      "title": "Cycling in Modern Cities",
      "text": "In recent years, many cities have started to encourage people to cycle instead of driving. This change is (1) _____ to improve air quality and reduce traffic jams in busy areas. For many commuters, cycling is a (2) _____ way to get to work while also getting some exercise. However, some cyclists feel that the roads are still not (3) _____ enough for them. To solve this, city planners are (4) _____ new bike lanes that are separated from car traffic. These lanes make it much easier for people to (5) _____ their destination safely. If more people choose to cycle, our cities will become much quieter and (6) _____ places to live in the future.",
